---
import Section from './Section.astro'
// Manifold Server. IN BETA and not generally available — every mention must say
// so, and nothing here may promise a date.
//
// Two hard constraints on this copy:
//  1. vippsas/manifold-server is an INTERNAL repo with no LICENSE. Do NOT link
//     it (it 404s for everyone) and do NOT call it open source. Only the desktop
//     app is MIT.
//  2. Its README documents the operator's own deployment — cloud subscriptions,
//     key vaults, clusters, service catalogues. None of that belongs on a public
//     page. Describe the behaviour, never the infrastructure.
//
// This section is also the honest exception to the hero claim: running the
// server IS the one case where code leaves your machine. Saying so plainly is
// more persuasive than a seamless claim, because it leaves for infrastructure
// *you* control rather than a vendor's.
---
<Section id="server" eyebrow="Manifold Server" badge="Beta">
  <Fragment slot="title">
    Issues in. <em>Pull requests out</em>.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    Label a GitHub issue and a server you run works it to a pull request — with nobody
    watching the terminal.
  </Fragment>

  <p class="availability">
    <b>Not released yet.</b> Manifold Server is in beta and isn't published — you can't
    download or run it today, and there's no date. The desktop app above is the shipping
    product and never depends on it. This is here so you know where Manifold is going.
  </p>

  <div class="mono-figure boxed">
    <pre>  <b>issue labelled</b>    manifold
        │
  <b>claimed</b>           manifold-working    <span class="dim">a label swap, so two</span>
        │                                 <span class="dim">runners never collide</span>
  <b>sandboxed</b>         clone → branch manifold/issue-&lt;n&gt;
        │
  <b>agent runs</b>        unattended, with a time limit
        │
  <b>verify</b>            your command — compile, unit, contract
        │
  <b>pull request</b>      "Closes #&lt;n&gt;"  ·  manifold-done
        │
        └── <span class="dim">failed, or changed nothing →</span> needs-human <span class="dim">+ why</span></pre>
  </div>

  <p class="body">
    A run that fails, or that changes nothing, escalates with a comment explaining why.
    It does not open a speculative pull request.
  </p>

  <p class="body">
    The verify command is yours, and it runs offline in the same locked-down sandbox as the
    agent — so a green result means compile-and-unit sound, not integration-proven. A
    non-zero exit blocks the pull request rather than shipping something broken.
  </p>

  <p class="pull">Humans stay the merge gate. The server opens pull requests; your CI and branch protection decide what lands.</p>

  <p class="body">
    Concurrency is capped, because concurrency is spend. Each agent invocation has a
    time limit. Commits land under the bot's own identity, and the repo-controlled verify
    command runs with the git credentials stripped from its environment.
  </p>

  <div class="caveat">
    <p>
      <b>This is the one place your code leaves your Mac</b> — into a container
      <em>you</em> deploy, with <em>your</em> GitHub and model credentials. There is still
      no account, and still no service of ours in the middle. Running it is entirely
      optional; the desktop app never needs it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="note">
    Want it? Start a thread in
    <a href="https://github.com/vippsas/manifold/discussions">Discussions</a>, or reach out
    on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/svenmalvik/">LinkedIn</a>.
  </p>
</Section>

<style>
  .body { color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: var(--measure); margin-top: var(--space-xl); }
  .pull {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-gold);
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  /* Availability first, before any capability copy — a reader who skims must not
     come away thinking this ships today. */
  .availability {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-gold);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 var(--frame-highlight);
  }
  .availability b { color: var(--text-primary); }

  .caveat {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-cyan);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 var(--frame-highlight);
  }
  .caveat p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .caveat b { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .caveat em { font-style: italic; color: var(--accent-text); }

  .note { margin-top: var(--space-lg); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.76rem; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: var(--measure); }
</style>
